      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Description</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <p>
            A pair of Heras rail fences bar and separate the entrance to the field
            from the track owned by {{ FF }} over which {{ FFH }} holds a right
            of access. The entrance to the field is secured by one or more large
            and immovable barriers when required to prevent unauthorised access,
            which in past years has resulted in:
          </p>
          <ol type="i">
            <li>fly-tipping of hundreds of tyres;</li>
            <li>dumping of plastics and contaminated waste;</li>
            <li>damage to protected features;</li>
            <li>criminal damage; and</li>
            <li>theft.</li>
          </ol>
        </td></tr>
      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Defence Response to Claims Made</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <strong>Health and safety risk:</strong>
              It is unknown how the secured fence, which prevents unauthorised
              access, constitutes a risk to public health and safety.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Nuisance:</strong>
              It is unknown how the fence, which does not intrude upon the right
              of way enjoyed by {{ FFH }}, constitutes a nuisance.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Unsightliness:</strong>
              It is unknown how unsightliness — which is in any case a subjective
              term — is relevant to {{ FFH }}, particularly given that the fence
              cannot be seen from the {{ FFH }} title, and that it is performing
              the functional purpose of limiting access to {{ FF }} property.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

